% Where a retained page's marks were held, said by the run that held them.
%
% A page too large for the band budget is held as the marks that made it.
% Where those marks go is a decision about the machine rather than about
% the page -- in memory while they come to less than the raster banding
% saves, in a scratch file past that, or wherever the invocation said --
% and this is the page that says which happened.
%
% M says how much is drawn, and is the whole of the difference between
% the two shapes this is run in. A light drawing keeps the marks well
% under the raster banding saves and a heavy one carries them far past
% it, so the same page asked at two sizes asks both sides of the rule.
%
% Nothing here decides anything. What is printed is a measurement, and
% the page itself is written out so that a wrapper can hold every state
% to putting out the same bytes: where a page's marks were kept is not
% something a page shows.

/num { 20 string cvs } bind def
/ID 1183615869 internaldict def

/M where { pop }{ /M 200 def } ifelse

/isrec { DEVICE /.playclass known } bind def
/saving { isrec { DEVICE ID /.recordsaving get exec }{ 0 } ifelse } bind def
/cost { isrec { DEVICE ID /.recordcost get exec exch pop exch pop }{ 0 } ifelse } bind def

/W 2550 def
/H 3300 def
<< /PageSize [W H] >> setpagedevice

% A grid, so that every band of the page carries ink: a band holding
% nothing but the ground is a band the loop does not paint, and a page
% whose ink is in one band is a page held whole for every purpose here.
/draw {
    gsave 0 setgray
    /g M sqrt cvi def
    0 1 g 1 sub {
        /i exch def
        0 1 g 1 sub {
            /j exch def
            i W mul g div 2 add
            j H mul g div 3 add
            2 2 rectfill
        } for
    } for
    grestore
} bind def

draw

(BAND ) print currentsystemparams /CurBandHeight get num print (\n) print
(SAVING ) print saving num print (\n) print
(COST ) print cost num print (\n) print
(SPILL ) print currentsystemparams /RecordSpill get num print (\n) print
(WHERE ) print currentsystemparams /CurRecordSpill get num print (\n) print

showpage
(\nDONE\n) print
flush
